      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes how the guarded write path implements a rollback mechanism for file writes. Here are the key points:\n\n- **Prior state recording**: Before overwriting any file, the system records its previous state\u2014either the existing content or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist\u2014into an in-memory write journal.\n\n- **Rollback on failure**: If the agent run fails (due to turn cap being exceeded, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back all recorded writes in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed, or deleting newly created files.\n\n- **All-or-nothing semantics**: This provides transaction-like semantics for writes without requiring a database\u2014the journal itself serves as the transaction log, held in memory for the duration of a single run.\n\n- **Query agent exclusion**: The Query agent never uses the rollback path since it doesn\u0027t have a write tool available.",
